From ff7477ab0a23c97e1b5fa65bc414fd88a7715171 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bentrd <benj.tordjman@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:41:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wiki: document the Strain Creation API, with a Your First
 Strain tutorial

New page Your First Strain walks through a strain end to end (Overtime:
after ten turns in a game, every turn costs $1): project setup, a
StrainBehaviour with per-game state, registering in OnEnable and
unregistering in OnDisable, the hook table and when each fires (the
"started" hooks never fire on Continue), writing strain text in the game's
markup, incompatible strains, testing with 'strain apply', reading the
game's own strains, and publishing with the registry's "strains" list.

API Reference gains a Gambonanza.StrainApi section: StrainBuilder (heat
and icons included), the hooks, StrainBehaviour, every Strains member, and how the API follows the
run from GameManager state changes. Console Commands lists the 'strain'
family; Example Mods, Home, the sidebar, How Modding Works, Publishing
Your Mod (the "strains" field and tag) and Troubleshooting ("My strain
does nothing") point at it.
