+## `Gambonanza.StrainApi`
+
+The Strain Creation API, a library mod like GambitApi. A **strain** is one of
+the game's run modifiers - No Queen, Tile Exhauster, Time is money! - picked
+before a run and in force for all of it. StrainApi lets a mod add its own.
+Reference `Gambonanza.StrainApi.dll`, add `"dependencies": ["StrainApi"]` to
+your `mod.json`, and build strains with `StrainBuilder`. Walkthrough:
+[Your First Strain](Your-First-Strain).
+
+Modded strains go on the game's own Custom strain screen: StrainApi adds arrows
+either side of the STRAINS title that page over to **MOD STRAINS**, 15 cards a
+page, drawn like the game's own. Their heat counts on the gauge like any other
+strain (and may take it past 30). They come with Custom runs only; the preset
+difficulties are left alone. The console's `strain on <id>` picks too. Picks
+lock in when the next run starts, and the run keeps them - through quitting
+and continuing - until another run starts.
+
+Three words, used precisely throughout: **registered** (a loaded mod defined
+it this session), **selected** (the player picked it for their next run - a
+saved preference), **active** (it is on the run being played right now).
+
+### The one-strain example
+
+```csharp
+using Gambonanza.StrainApi;
+
+StrainBuilder.Create("taxman")
+    .WithName("Taxman")
+    .WithDescription("Every game costs <color=*>$1</color> to start.")
+    .OnGameStart(strain => PayTheTaxman())
+    .Register();
+```
+
+Registering needs nothing from the game, so it is immediate and works from
+`OnLoad`. Registering in `OnEnable` and calling `Strains.Unregister(id)` in
+`OnDisable` makes a strain mod hot-toggleable.
+
+### `StrainBuilder`
+
+Every method returns `this`; only `Create(id)` (first) and `Register()` (last)
+are required.
+
+| Call | Notes |
+| ---- | ----- |
+| `Create(string id)` | Lowercase letters, digits, `-` and `_`, up to 40 characters. **Permanent**: the player's picks and saved runs refer to it. |
+| `.WithName(string)` | Display name. Defaults to the id. |
+| `.WithDescription(string)` | One sentence, in the game's markup (`<color=*>$1</color>`). The card's tooltip renders it like the game's own; the console shows it as plain text. |
+| `.WithHeat(int)` | What the strain adds to the heat gauge, like the game's own (1 to 3). 0 to `Strains.MaxHeat` (9); defaults to 1. |
+| `.WithIconFile(string path)` | The card's icon, a PNG in your mod's folder (path relative to it). Point-filtered; the game's own strain icons are 33x27 pixel art. |
+| `.WithIcon(Sprite)` / `.WithGameIcon(string spriteName)` | The icon as a sprite you made, or borrowed from one of the game's sprites by name. With none of the three, the card shows a question mark. |
+| `.IncompatibleWith(params string[] ids)` | Picking either side unpicks the other. One side is enough; unknown ids are fine. |
+| `.WithBehaviour<T>()` | `T : StrainBehaviour`, spawned while the strain is active. |
+| `.OnActivate` / `.OnDeactivate` | `Action<StrainBehaviour>` around the strain's stay on a run. |
+| `.OnRunStart` / `.OnGameStart` / `.OnPlayerTurn` / `.OnGameEnd` / `.OnShopOpen` | `Action<StrainBehaviour>`, see the hook table below. |
+| `.Build()` | The `StrainDefinition` without registering it. |
+| `.Register()` | Builds and registers it; returns the definition, or `null` if it was rejected (bad or duplicate id, abstract behaviour type - the log says why). |
+
+### The hooks
+
+A strain uses the builder delegates, a `StrainBehaviour` subclass, or both (the
+override runs first). An exception in any hook is logged and contained - it
+never reaches the game or another strain.
+
+| Override | Builder | When |
+| -------- | ------- | ---- |
+| `Awake` / `Start` | `.OnActivate` | The strain came alive on the run: a new run started with it, or a saved run with it was continued. |
+| `OnRunStarted()` | `.OnRunStart` | A **new** run started with it. Once per run, never on Continue: the place for one-time changes to the run itself (money, pieces, gambits), which the game saves with the run. |
+| `OnGameStarted()` | `.OnGameStart` | A game (one match) began. Once per game. |
+| `OnPlayerTurn()` | `.OnPlayerTurn` | The start of each of the player's turns (`TurnManager.OnPlayerTurn`). |
+| `OnGameEnded()` | `.OnGameEnd` | The game is over: won, lost, or left mid-way. |
+| `OnShopOpened()` | `.OnShopOpen` | The shop opened after a game. |
+| `OnDestroy` | `.OnDeactivate` | Put away: the player left the run, the strain was taken off it, it was unregistered, or StrainApi was disabled. |
+
+"Started" hooks fire only when something actually starts. Continuing a saved
+run gives no `OnRunStarted`, and continuing into the middle of a game or the
+shop gives no `OnGameStarted` / `OnShopOpened` (that game still gets its
+`OnGameEnded`). `Awake`/`Start` run either way; `Strains.IsGameInProgress`
+tells you whether you came back mid-game.
+
+### `StrainBehaviour`
+
+```csharp
+public abstract class StrainBehaviour : MonoBehaviour
+{
+    public StrainDefinition Definition { get; }   // set before Awake runs
+    public string Id { get; }
+    protected virtual void OnRunStarted();
+    protected virtual void OnGameStarted();
+    protected virtual void OnPlayerTurn();
+    protected virtual void OnGameEnded();
+    protected virtual void OnShopOpened();
+    protected void Log(string message);           // [StrainApi] [<id>] message
+}
+```
+
+One instance per active strain, on its own hidden GameObject that lives
+exactly as long as the strain is on the run being played. So `Start` /
+`OnDestroy` bracket the strain the way they bracket a gambit's ownership, and
+anything that takes an owner can take `this` - a CrumbleApi handle, say
+([Extra Strains' `ShortFuseStrain.cs`](https://github.com/ben-gambo/mods/blob/main/ExtraStrains/src/ShortFuseStrain.cs)).
+
+### `Strains`
+
+| Member | Meaning |
+| ------ | ------- |
+| `All`, `Get(id)`, `IsRegistered(id)` | The registry, in registration order. |
+| `Register(def)`, `Unregister(id)` | `Unregister` puts an active strain away first; the player's pick and the saved run keep the id, so registering it again brings everything back. |
+| `IsSelected(id)`, `Selected`, `SetSelected(id, bool)`, `ClearSelection()` | The picks for the next run. Picking one unpicks its incompatibles. Never touches the run being played. |
+| `IsRunInProgress`, `IsGameInProgress` | From a run starting or being continued until the player leaves it for the main menu; a game being played within it. |
+| `IsActive(id)`, `Active` | Strains on the run being played. |
+| `GetBehaviour(id)`, `GetBehaviour<T>()` | The live behaviour of an active strain. |
+| `Apply(id, out error)`, `Remove(id, out error)` | Put a strain on (or take it off) the run being played, now. `Apply` gives it what a run started with it would have seen by now: activation, `OnRunStarted`, and `OnGameStarted` if a game is on. The saved run remembers. For testing and cheats. |
+| `IsVanillaActive(Strain)`, `VanillaActive` | The game's own strains, read from the flag the game checks (`StrainManager.ActivatedStrain`): `Strains.IsVanillaActive(Strain.TILE_EXHAUST)`. Between runs it still holds the last run's. |
+| `IsBound` | StrainApi has found the game's `GameManager` and is following it. |
+| `OnRunStarted`, `OnRunResumed`, `OnRunLeft`, `OnSelectionChanged` | Events. `OnRunLeft` fires on the way back to the main menu, whether the player quit, lost or won - the game does not say which, and a run left mid-way can still be continued. |
+
+### How it follows the run
+
+The game raises no "run started" event. StrainApi watches
+`GameManager.onStateChanged` (and polls `CurrentState`) and reads each state as
+a phase: `MENU` leaves the run (every way out of a run ends there), `LOAD_RUN`
+means Continue, `PIECE_SELECTION`/`BOARD_PLACEMENT`/`INGAME`/`WIN`/`RESULT`/
+`LOSE`/`SHOP` and the between-games screens only happen inside a run, and
+everything else - `PAUSE`, `SETTINGS`, `RUN_INFO`, `PROMOTION` - changes
+nothing (the game re-enters `INGAME` when they close; same game). A run state
+while not in a run starts a new run, unless the game just passed through
+`LOAD_RUN`. As a fallback, `ChessDataManager.CurrentWave` going backwards also
+means a new run. That logic lives in `RunTracker`, which is plain C# with unit
+tests: `dotnet test sample_mods/StrainApi/Tests`.
+
+Things to know:
+
+- The player's picks and the strains each run started with are saved to
+  `<Application.persistentDataPath>/GambonanzaMods/StrainApi.json` - outside
+  the mod folder, which the manager replaces on every update.
+- A strain whose mod is missing when a run is continued is skipped (and
+  logged); reinstalling the mod brings it back on the next Continue.
+- `wave set` to an earlier wave in the console looks like a new run to the
+  fallback above.
+- Like everything in this framework it binds to game members by name; a game
+  update that renames `StrainManager.ActivatedStrain`, `TurnManager.OnPlayerTurn`
+  or a `State` member breaks the build the way it breaks any mod compiled
+  against the game.
+
+---
+
