+### Strain Creation API
+
+Installed with any mod that adds strains. Picks made here are the same ones the
+MOD STRAINS page of the Custom strain screen shows.
+
+| Command | What it does |
+| ------- | ------------ |
+| `strain` | What is picked for your next run, and what is on the run in progress - the game's own strains included. |
+| `strain list` | Every modded strain, marked `[picked]` and `[on this run]`. |
+| `strain info <id>` | A strain's full description, the mod it comes from, and what it cannot be combined with. |
+| `strain on <id>` | Pick a strain for your next Custom run (unpicks anything it cannot be combined with). |
+| `strain off <id\|all>` | Unpick one, or all of them. |
+| `strain apply <id>` | Put a strain on the run you are playing, right now - it gets what a run started with it would have seen by now. The quickest way to try one. |
+| `strain remove <id>` | Take a strain off the run you are playing, right now. |
+
+Picks only ever change your *next* run; the run in progress keeps the strains it
+started with (use `apply`/`remove` for that). Ids tab-complete, and names work
+too: `strain on short fuse`. Full API:
+[API Reference](API-Reference#gambonanzastrainapi).
+
