+# Your First Strain
+
+A **strain** is one of the game's run modifiers: No Queen, Tile Exhauster,
+Heavy Landing, Time is money! The player picks them before a run and they hold
+for the whole of it. Vanilla keeps its strains in `StrainManager`.
+
+Custom strains go in through the **StrainApi** library mod, which gives you a
+fluent `StrainBuilder` in the same style as GambitApi's. By the end of this
+page you will have a working strain named **Overtime**: after ten turns in a
+game, every turn costs a dollar.
+
+Players pick modded strains on the game's own Custom strain screen - arrows
+either side of the STRAINS title page over to **MOD STRAINS** - or with
+`strain on <id>` in the console. They come with Custom runs only. Picks lock
+in when the next run starts, and the run keeps them - through quitting and
+continuing - until another run starts.
+
+Prerequisite: [Your First Mod](Your-First-Mod).
+
+---
+
+## 1. Project setup
+
+Create `sample_mods/Overtime/`, same shape as before. The csproj references
+`StrainApi` and the game's own code:
+
+```xml
+<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
+
+  <PropertyGroup>
+    <TargetFramework>netstandard2.1</TargetFramework>
+    <AssemblyName>Overtime</AssemblyName>
+    <RootNamespace>Overtime</RootNamespace>
+    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
+    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
+    <AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath>false</AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath>
+    <CopyLocalLockFileAssemblies>false</CopyLocalLockFileAssemblies>
+  </PropertyGroup>
+
+  <ItemGroup>
+    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\ModSdk\ModSdk.csproj">
+      <Private>false</Private>
+    </ProjectReference>
+    <ProjectReference Include="..\StrainApi\StrainApi.csproj">
+      <Private>false</Private>
+    </ProjectReference>
+  </ItemGroup>
+
+  <ItemGroup>
+    <Reference Include="Assembly-CSharp">
+      <HintPath>..\..\refs\Assembly-CSharp.dll</HintPath>
+      <Private>false</Private>
+    </Reference>
+    <Reference Include="UnityEngine.CoreModule">
+      <HintPath>..\..\refs\UnityEngine.CoreModule.dll</HintPath>
+      <Private>false</Private>
+    </Reference>
+  </ItemGroup>
+
+</Project>
+```
+
+`mod.json` - the **dependency** makes ModHost load StrainApi first:
+
+```json
+{
+    "id":           "Overtime",
+    "name":         "Overtime",
+    "version":      "1.0.0",
+    "author":       "you",
+    "entry":        "Overtime.OvertimeMod",
+    "enabled":      true,
+    "gameVersion":  ">=1.0",
+    "dependencies": ["StrainApi"],
+    "description":  "A strain: after ten turns in a game, every turn costs $1."
+}
+```
+
+---
+
+## 2. Write the strain
+
+A strain that keeps state gets a `StrainBehaviour` - a `MonoBehaviour` that
+StrainApi creates when a run starts with the strain on it (or a saved run with
+it is continued) and destroys when the player leaves that run. Its lifetime
+*is* the strain's stay on the run.
+
+`OvertimeStrain.cs`:
+
+```csharp
+using Blukulele.CHE;
+using Blukulele.Core;
+using Gambonanza.StrainApi;
+
+namespace Overtime
+{
+    /// <summary>After FreeTurns turns in a game, every turn costs $1.</summary>
+    public sealed class OvertimeStrain : StrainBehaviour
+    {
+        public const int FreeTurns = 10;
+
+        private int _turns;
+
+        // A fresh count for every game.
+        protected override void OnGameStarted() => _turns = 0;
+
+        protected override void OnPlayerTurn()
+        {
+            if (++_turns <= FreeTurns) return;
+            if (!SingletonMonoBehaviour<ChessDataManager>.IsCreated()) return;
+            var chess = SingletonMonoBehaviour<ChessDataManager>.Instance;
+            if (chess != null && chess.Coins >= 1) chess.DecreaseCoin(1);   // how the game spends money
+        }
+    }
+}
+```
+
+Two things to internalise:
+
+- **The hooks fire when something actually starts.** `OnGameStarted` runs once
+  per game; a run continued in the middle of a game does *not* get it again
+  (the game's own state was saved; yours was not). Here that means a continued
+  game restarts the count - fine for Overtime. If a strain must know it came
+  back mid-game, check `Strains.IsGameInProgress` in `Start`.
+- **Guard singletons.** `ChessDataManager` is not there on the title screen.
+  `IsCreated()` keeps the strain safe in every context.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Register it
+
+`OvertimeMod.cs`:
+
+```csharp
+using Gambonanza.ModSdk;
+using Gambonanza.StrainApi;
+
+namespace Overtime
+{
+    public sealed class OvertimeMod : IMod, IModLifecycle
+    {
+        public void OnLoad(IModContext ctx) { }
+
+        public void OnEnable()
+        {
+            StrainBuilder.Create("overtime")               // permanent: picks and saved runs use it
+                .WithName("Overtime")
+                .WithDescription($"After {OvertimeStrain.FreeTurns} turns in a game, every turn costs <color=*>$1</color>.")
+                .WithBehaviour<OvertimeStrain>()
+                .Register();
+        }
+
+        public void OnDisable() => Strains.Unregister("overtime");
+    }
+}
+```
+
+A strain needs nothing from the game to be registered, so registration is
+immediate and safe anywhere, `OnLoad` included. Doing it in `OnEnable` and
+unregistering in `OnDisable` is all it takes for `mods disable Overtime` to
+work mid-session: a strain on the run being played is put away cleanly, and
+the player's pick is kept for when it comes back.
+
+### The hooks
+
+Each exists both as a `StrainBehaviour` override and as a builder delegate
+(`.OnGameStart(strain => ...)`); the override runs first.
+
+| Override | Builder | When |
+| -------- | ------- | ---- |
+| `Awake` / `Start` | `.OnActivate` | The strain came alive on the run: a new run started with it, or a saved run with it was continued. Subscribe to game events, take handles. |
+| `OnRunStarted` | `.OnRunStart` | A **new** run started with it. Once per run, never on Continue - the place for one-time changes to the run itself. |
+| `OnGameStarted` | `.OnGameStart` | A game (one match) began. Once per game. |
+| `OnPlayerTurn` | `.OnPlayerTurn` | The start of each of the player's turns during a game. |
+| `OnGameEnded` | `.OnGameEnd` | The game is over: won, lost, or left mid-way. |
+| `OnShopOpened` | `.OnShopOpen` | The shop opened after a game. |
+| `OnDestroy` | `.OnDeactivate` | The strain is being put away: the player left the run, it was taken off, or StrainApi was disabled. Undo what activation set up. |
+
+### Writing strain text
+
+Descriptions use the game's own markup, which the mod manager renders the way
+the game does. Copy the vanilla strains' voice - one short sentence - and
+their colours:
+
+| Markup | Used by vanilla for |
+| ------ | ------------------- |
+| `<color=*>$1</color>` | money ("WAITING costs $1") |
+| `<color=©>LAND</color>` | landing ("You can only LAND a piece on the first row.") |
+| `<color=µ>WAITING</color>` | waiting |
+| `<shake>Crumble Mode</shake>` | the crumble |
+| `<sprite=10> <color=^>QUEEN</color>` | a piece, with its glyph |
+
+The card's tooltip renders the markup like the game's own strains; the console
+shows descriptions as plain text, so keep the sentence readable without the
+colours.
+
+### Heat and icon
+
+Every strain adds to the Custom screen's heat gauge. The game's own add 1 to 3;
+`.WithHeat(n)` sets yours (default 1). The card's icon is `.WithIconFile("overtime.png")`,
+a PNG next to your DLL - pixel art at the game's own 33x27 fits best - or
+`.WithGameIcon("SPR_Ascend_Lock")` to borrow one of the game's sprites. Without
+either, the card shows a question mark.
+
+### `WithBehaviour<T>()` vs builder delegates
+
+Stateless strains don't need a class. [Extra Strains](https://github.com/ben-gambo/mods/tree/main/ExtraStrains)' **Taxman** is
+the whole strain:
+
+```csharp
+StrainBuilder.Create("taxman")
+    .WithName("Taxman")
+    .WithDescription("Every game costs <color=*>$1</color> to start.")
+    .WithHeat(1)
+    .WithIconFile("taxman.png")
+    .OnGameStart(_ => PayTheTaxman())
+    .Register();
+```
+
+The moment you need a field (a counter, a flag, a handle), write a
+`StrainBehaviour`. Both can be combined.
+
+### Strains that cannot be combined
+
+```csharp
+.IncompatibleWith("taxman", "some-other-mods-strain")
+```
+
+Picking either side for the next run unpicks the other. Declaring it on one
+side is enough, and unknown ids are fine - the rule applies once both are
+registered.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Build, install, test
+
+```bash
+./sample_mods/build.sh --install
+```
+
+In game, open the console (<kbd>`</kbd> / <kbd>F10</kbd>):
+
+```
+strain list               confirm it registered
+strain on overtime        pick it for your next run
+strain                    what is picked, and what is on the run in progress
+```
+
+Then start a run. Or, to skip that, start one first and put the strain on it
+right now:
+
+```
+strain apply overtime     on the run you are playing, immediately
+strain remove overtime    and off again
+```
+
+`strain apply` gives the strain what a run started with it would have seen by
+now: activation, `OnRunStarted`, and `OnGameStarted` if a game is on. For the
+real thing, pick it on the Custom strain screen (the arrows by STRAINS) and
+start a run.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Play nicely with the game's own strains
+
+`Strains.IsVanillaActive(Strain.X)` reads the flag the game itself checks
+(`StrainManager.ActivatedStrain`), for a strain - or a gambit - that should
+defer to a vanilla one:
+
+```csharp
+// Vanilla "Time is money!" already charges for waiting; don't double-dip.
+if (Strains.IsVanillaActive(Strain.COSTLY_WAIT)) return;
+```
+
+`strain` in the console lists the game's strains on the run in progress
+alongside the modded ones.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Publish it
+
+Two extras matter for strain mods:
+
+- **Fill in the `strains` array in your registry entry**, and tag it
+  `strains`. The manager shows each strain on your mod's page - name, and its
+  rule in the game's colours - so players know what they are picking. Mirror
+  what you passed to `StrainBuilder`:
+  ```json
+  "tags": ["strains", "gameplay"],
+  "strains": [
+    { "id": "overtime", "name": "Overtime",
+      "description": "After 10 turns in a game, every turn costs <color=*>$1</color>." }
+  ]
+  ```
+- **Depend on `strain-api`** in the entry, so the manager installs it first.
+
+Everything else: [Publishing Your Mod](Publishing-Your-Mod).
+
+---
+
+## Common pitfalls
+
+- **Ids are forever.** The player's picks and their saved run refer to the
+  strain by the id passed to `Create`. Ids are lowercase letters, digits, `-`
+  and `_`; anything else is rejected with a log line.
+- **Undo live changes, not run changes.** Money, pieces and gambits you change
+  in `OnRunStarted` are part of the run, and the game saves them with it -
+  leave them. Event subscriptions, handles and anything else you set up in
+  `Awake`/`Start` must be undone in `OnDestroy`.
+- **Don't count on `OnGameStarted` after Continue.** See section 2.
+- **Picks live outside your mod folder** (`<persistentDataPath>/GambonanzaMods/StrainApi.json`),
+  because the manager replaces a mod's folder when it updates it. You never
+  need to touch that file.
+- **Modded strains only come with Custom runs.** They live on their own pages
+  of the Custom strain screen; the preset difficulties (Pawn to King) and the
+  medals know nothing about them.
